+## Intent
+
+**Problem:** QoS is invisible. With a pipe selected, `1/2` picks a class and `E/S/B` assigns its lane, and right-click cycles an opaque emphasis dial (3.2, presets from `balance.json`). Players cannot see what any of it does — the mechanic exists but is illegible.
+
+**Approach:** Replace the invisible dial with a real per-pipe **QoS panel** (selecting a pipe shows it): per-type rows (class → lane, clickable or `E/S/B`), the resulting lane split with real numbers, and a manual-edit affordance. **Auto-reservation (default):** the split follows the player's type→lane assignments from a fixed ladder (`lane_auto_reserve_ladder` in balance.json: 1 lane = 100 · 2 = 70/30 · 3 = 50/30/20). **Manual override:** a per-pipe weight editor; manual pipes are marked in the panel and revertible to auto. The type→lane call stays 100% player-owned (08-12 canon); only the split auto-follows.
+
+## Boundaries & Constraints
+
+**Always:**
+- The type→lane call stays player-owned — every type rides Standard until the player categorizes it (08-12 canon, load-pinned in catalog.odin).
+- Replay equality `[E10]` by construction: weight changes happen ONLY through the serialized command path (`Cmd_Set_Emphasis`), never as unlogged app-side mutation. Auto-ladder and manual editor both write through it.
+- `Cmd_Set_Emphasis` evolves its payload from `preset: u16` → `weights: [3]i32` (same serialized tag 5; LOG_VERSION 3→4). **Not a new command kind** — the "no new command kinds" scope guard holds. (User ruling via lavish clarify, 2026-08-14.)
+- Ladder lane-count semantics (user ruling via lavish clarify, 2026-08-14): **in-play lanes = the lanes the player assigned + Standard (always reserved)** — Standard is the default home of every un-categorized type. Untouched pipes keep the current catalog default preset, so no-QoS-edit runs stay byte-stable (only the catalog-hash fold shifts — the 4.3 provable-fold discipline).
+- Ladder is data-driven (`lane_auto_reserve_ladder` in balance.json, fail-fast validated, ODN-5), integer weights (ODN-10), `0 ≤ w ≤ MAX_WEIGHT`, never all-zero (E5 fallback stays the allocator's guard).
+- E6 never-drop guard preserved: a never-drop class may not be parked on (or a weight edit may not zero) its lane.
+- No maps in core (ODN-10); core stays pure (ODN-1); render strings ASCII-only (lint gate 6).
+- Full local suite green before PR: `odin test core`, `tools/lint.sh`, `tools/harness.sh run`.
+
+**Ask First:**
+- (none pending — both design rulings received; if a new ruling-shaped decision arises mid-build, HALT and ask)
+
+**Never:**
+- No new command kinds; no economy; no advanced-mode gating (document as `[ASSUMPTION]` — future knob, do not build); no node-triage UI (junctions forward per-packet, canon); no balance retuning.
+- Do NOT re-amend the canon (GDD M2 / ODN-3 amend already on v2, commit `5f51236`). If the implementation needs a different ladder value, STOP and flag — do not change the docs.
+- No non-ASCII in render string literals (the byte-truncating draw_text_c — mojibake ships into blessed T2s).
+
+## I/O & Edge-Case Matrix
+
+| Scenario | Input / State | Expected Output / Behavior | Error Handling |
+|----------|--------------|---------------------------|----------------|
+| Untouched pipe | no lane overrides, no weight edit | pipe keeps catalog default preset weights; no sparse QoS bytes (T1 stable) | n/a |
+| One lane in play | `streaming→Express` (email on Standard default) | in-play = {Express, Standard} = 2 → `[70,30,0]` (Express 70 / Standard 30) | n/a |
+| Three lanes in play | `streaming→Express` + `email→Best-effort` | in-play = {E, S, B} = 3 → `[50,30,20]` (Express exactly 50%) | n/a |
+| Manual override | panel weight editor sets e.g. `[60,25,15]` | `Cmd_Set_Emphasis{weights}` logged; panel marks pipe manual; serialization + lane widths follow | weights out of domain → `.Invalid_Weights` (bus reject, HUD toast) |
+| Revert to auto | manual pipe, player hits revert | overrides recompute ladder weights via `Cmd_Set_Emphasis`; manual marker clears | n/a |
+| Never-drop class | bank class parked on a zeroed lane / weight edit zeroes its lane | edit rejected `.Invalid_Weights` (E6) — never silent | HUD toast |
+| All-zero weights | manual editor sets `[0,0,0]` | rejected at the bus (E5 fallback is the allocator's guard, not a user state) | `.Invalid_Weights` |
+| Ladder config drift | balance.json ladder malformed/missing | fail-fast catalog load error, named field | startup abort (ODN-5) |
