+# Story 5.8 — QoS panel + assignment-driven auto-reservation
+
+Makes QoS legible (user ruling 2026-08-14): a per-pipe **QoS panel** replaces
+the invisible emphasis dial. Selecting a pipe shows per-type lane rows, the
+resulting lane split with real numbers, and a manual weight editor.
+**Auto-reservation (default):** the split follows the player's type→lane
+assignments from a fixed data-driven ladder (1 lane = 100 · 2 = 70/30 ·
+3 = 50/30/20 in `balance.json`). **Manual override (advanced path):** a
+per-pipe weight editor — manual pipes are marked + revertible to auto. The
+type→lane call stays 100% player-owned (08-12 canon); only the split
+auto-follows.
+
+Story card: `_bmad-output/planning-artifacts/sprints/stories-v2.md` § Story 5.8.
+Canon amend (GDD M2 lever #2 + arch ODN-3 + ladder field) is **already on v2**
+(commit `5f51236`, the slice-5 rulings commit) — this PR implements it, it does
+not re-amend.
+
+## Decisions & rationale
+
+- **`Cmd_Set_Emphasis` payload evolves `preset: u16` → `weights: [3]i32`**
+  (same serialized tag; LOG_VERSION 3→4). The user-ruled design requires the
+  auto-ladder AND the manual editor to write the computed split through the
+  SAME serialized command so replay equality `[E10]` holds by construction —
+  a preset index can't carry a computed weight set. **Not a new command kind**
+  (scope guard holds). Ruled via lavish clarify 2026-08-14. Golden re-bless
+  is the documented LOG_VERSION fold.
+- **Ladder lane-count semantics (ruled A):** in-play lanes = the lanes the
+  player assigned + **Standard** (always reserved — the default home of every
+  un-categorized type, canon-safe). Untouched pipes keep the catalog default
+  preset (byte-stable no-QoS goldens). Consequence: `streaming→Express` alone
+  (email left on Standard) = 2 lanes in play → **70/30**; adding
+  `email→Best-effort` = 3 lanes → **50/30/20** (Express exactly 50% — the
+  story's launchable example + the 3-lane golden). The ladder's 1-lane row
+  (100%) applies to the all-assignments-on-Standard edge.
+- **Right-click dial retired (documented choice):** the 3.2 emphasis dial's
+  only job was cycling opaque presets. Right-click on a pipe now selects it
+  and opens/refreshes the panel; the panel's per-type row clicks + `1/2` +
+  `E/S/B` + the manual editor replace cycling. The catalog presets remain as
+  manual quick-set chips (a preset is a weight set).
+- **Auto/manual mode is DERIVED, never stored:** a pipe is manual iff its
+  current weights differ from `qos_auto_weights(its assignments)` — no extra
+  serialized state; revert = write the auto set back. Lane assignments always
+  auto-follow (the assignment path IS the auto path); the editor is entered
+  explicitly via `[Edit weights]`.
+- **Legible text (user note 2026-08-14):** the full font story is later; the
+  panel uses the existing renderer at legible sizes (>= 14px), strong
+  ink/ink_soft contrast on the cream card, ASCII-only literals (lint gate 6).
+- **`[ASSUMPTION]`** — harder-eras / advanced-mode gating of manual editing
+  is a FUTURE knob, not built. `[ASSUMPTION]` — 2-class MVP roster
+  (email + streaming); the 3-lane golden exercises both assignments.
+  `[ASSUMPTION]` — the manual editor nudges weights in ±5 steps, no sum
+  invariant (WFQ weights are arbitrary integers — the presets [4,2,1] don't
+  sum to 100 either; the % readout is derived).
+- **Golden fold (4.3 provable, not assumed):** every existing `.log.bin`
+  diff = the LOG_VERSION byte + the 8 catalog-hash bytes only; all T2 PNGs
+  byte-identical; 2 new demos (qos_auto 3-lane 50/30/20, qos_manual 60/25/15)
+  with T2 captures (lane widths visibly re-split).
+
+## Verification
+
+- `odin test core` — 167 tests green (incl. new ladder-semantics pins,
+  never-drop-safety, command-shape bus guards, replay equality)
+- `tools/lint.sh` — all §16.3 gates green
+- `tools/harness.sh run` — 27 demos green (25 existing + 2 new), replay gate
+  passes for every blessed log
+- `git diff` golden proof — see above; T2 PNGs byte-identical for all
+  existing captures
